  "narrative": "The new battery produced several far stronger contrasts than the prior marker screen, so the audit needed to distinguish true threshold-exceeding associations from near-threshold multiplicity artifacts and opposite-direction coding effects. All claims H13-H24 were registered in the negative raw direction, i.e. exposed level 1 has a more negative outcome_001 value and therefore stronger dependency. Under that convention, positive signed estimates support the registered stronger-dependency hypothesis, while negative signed estimates indicate an opposite raw association. H15 (feature_037=1 vs 0) is clearly accepted: signed estimate +0.804, 95% interval +0.742 to +0.867, both the point estimate and the full interval far exceed the +0.15 threshold. This is much larger than the previous marker effects and is unlikely to be a multiplicity artifact. H21 (feature_063=1 vs 0) is threshold-relevant but less certain: signed estimate +0.239, interval +0.145 to +0.332. The point estimate exceeds 0.15, but the lower bound is just below threshold, so I keep it unresolved and active, and request independent validation because this is the result where validation could be most decisive. H18 (feature_003=1 vs 0) is also near threshold: signed estimate +0.139, interval +0.065 to +0.213. Because the point is below the threshold and this is part of a 24-test screen, I keep it unresolved and deferred rather than actively pursuing it immediately. H13 and H17 show large opposite associations: feature_010=1 gives signed estimate -0.829, interval -0.891 to -0.767, and feature_002=1 gives signed estimate -0.810, interval -0.875 to -0.745. These reject the original stronger-dependency claims but indicate strong raw positive differences (weaker dependency in the exposed level). I therefore registered reversed claims rather than reinterpret the original directions. H14, H16, H19, H20, H22, H23, and H24 are small, null, or incompatible with a threshold-relevant effect. A key caution is that these binary predictors may be correlated or represent overlapping latent group structure; the current main-effect screen does not establish independent effects or causal relationships. Future follow-up should disentangle overlapping predictors and assess interactions only where scientifically useful.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 2 appraise: The binary main-effect screen now contains one clear accepted dataset-specific association: feature_037=1 versus 0 has signed effect +0.804 [0.742,0.867], far above threshold for stronger dependency in the claimed negative raw direction (H15 accepted, active). H21 (feature_063) is borderline active: +0.239 [0.145,0.332], point above threshold but lower slightly below; validation requested. H18 (feature_003) is near-threshold unresolved deferred: +0.139 [0.065,0.213]. Large opposite raw effects: feature_010 (R13 signed -0.829) and feature_002 (R17 signed -0.810). Original claims rejected; reversed proposals registered. Remaining binary screens H25-H35 and nominal H36 should still be tested, but priority now includes reversed feature_010 and feature_002 and any conditional or interaction analyses to understand overlap among feature_010, feature_002, feature_037, and feature_063. Need critical attention to correlated predictors: main effects alone cannot separate overlapping binary flags. No causal or biological interpretation yet. If validation for H21 is delivered, reassess H21 immediately; if validation fails or is inconclusive, keep it deferred/reject depending on interval. If reversed feature_010/feature_002 analyses confirm, accept those reversed claims as dataset-specific weaker-dependency associations. Continue broad screen only if these central signals do not consume all useful budget; otherwise follow up the discovered predictors."
